Z||000007||AkursedX||04-02-2001||11:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>My Fiero has turned a lot of heads... but I haven't gotten a date because of it yet!<P>My uncle's teal LaBaron GTC convertible attracts a lot of women!  Drive anywhere in that car with the top down and women in the area, and your sure to hear tons of compliments about the car!  Its crazy, but it happens all the time.  Must be the color!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Those Lebaron Convertibles are like the dream cars to girls.  I know about 10 different girls who think those are the greatest cars!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  I have not a clue as to why, besides the convertible part.  Girls love convertibles.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||04-03-2001||12:23 AM||||The women who don't like your car aren't worth it anyway.  Gotta find a woman who likes cars herself.  Granted, they aren't as common as car guys, but a car gal is a grand find.  Take the little lady I know, who happens to be my best friend in the world.  She had a 78 Firebird with a built 327 Vette motor in it, and really digs my Fiero!  The two of us can drink almost anyone under the table (we're almost afraid to see which of us would win, but I think I've got the edge.  It wouldn't be pretty!), and I'd let her cover me in a bar fight any night.  And on the other side, put her in an evening gown, and watch out!  The lady is, what people like to call, multi-faceted.  There's gotta be more than a handful of women out there like that.  We've just got to find them.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tina||04-03-2001||01:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AkursedX:<BR><B> Those Lebaron Convertibles are like the dream cars to girls.  I know about 10 different girls who think those are the greatest cars!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  I have not a clue as to why, besides the convertible part.  Girls love convertibles.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Teal is good.<BR>But could it be the "Hair-Snag-Factor" ?<BR>Although, I have never put the Chrysler Lebaron through the test. This could be the reason for it's popularity.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Tina<BR>||||reg||1
